    - Normalized eye crops to a fixed 128×128 resolution for CNN training.
    - Built a fullscreen dataset collection tool with moving gaze targets.
    - Automatically saved eye images with corresponding screen-coordinate labels.
    - Generated a labeled gaze dataset (currently ~1200 samples).
    - Refactored the project into two independent approaches:
    - eyetrackerv1: Geometry-based gaze estimation using handcrafted features.
    - eyetrackerv2: Appearance-based CNN pipeline for end-to-end gaze prediction.
    - Organized project structure for future model training and inference.

    Current Status:
    - Stable eye crop generation achieved.
    - Dataset collection pipeline operational.
    - Ready to begin CNN model implementation and training.

    Known limitations:
    - Current dataset was collected without head-pose normalization.
    - Data augmentation, train/validation split, and CNN training are pending.
